cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use TerraPulse or its outputs, please cite it as below."
title: "TerraPulse: NISAR L-band surface change mapping and interactive web app"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Sudais
    family-names: Khalid
  - given-names: Sunnia
    family-names: Aslam
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-13
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/sudais-khalid/terrapulse"
url: "https://sudais-khalid.github.io/terrapulse/"
abstract: >-
  TerraPulse turns NASA-ISRO NISAR L-band GCOV radar time series into web-ready
  layers of open water, likely flooded vegetation, change and seasonal rhythm,
  calibrated per radar mode on permanent water against never-flooded land and
  flagged for wind and heavy rain. Layers are published as a STAC catalog and
  explored in an open-source web app, with study sites on the lower Indus
  (Sindh, Pakistan) and the Amazon at Manaus (Brazil).
keywords:
  - NISAR
  - synthetic aperture radar
  - L-band
  - flood mapping
  - wetlands
  - change detection
  - STAC
  - NASA Space Apps Challenge
